          "source_text_sha256": "f0ea2f6c0cfa956fc7f7dee140924eb3dd8c61c1f05096c45532eefc5cb4cc18",
          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On June 20, 2006, at 11:30 PM, a witness in the Fontainebleau forest was intrigued by the passage of a white-cream glowing disk in the sky. The trajectory was straight from West to East with a steady speed. No particular noise was heard during the two to three-minute observation. This peculiar phenomenon of a glowing point passing through the sky, according to the direction of the wind, suggests a Thai lantern, likely released during a solstice celebration. The oval shape, the cream color (the observer is in complete darkness, any light seems white) are consistent with this hypothesis. The GEIPAN classifies this case as \"B\": probable observation of a Thai lantern.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "5890bfa740d79d9617e716629be61b36f5b4c8da22ad30632d3ba9dde288a78b"
        }
